AuthController API Endpoints

1. POST /api/auth/login
Request Body:
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "yourPassword"
}
Possible Responses:
- 200 OK
  {
    "token": "jwt_token_string",
    "name": "User Name",
    "isFirstTimeLogin": false,
    "message": "Login successful",
    "role": "User",
    "otpRequired": false
  }
- 401 Unauthorized
  "Invalid credentials or inactive account"
- 400 Bad Request
  Model validation errors (missing email/password, invalid email format)

2. POST /api/auth/verify-otp
Request Body:
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "otpCode": 123456
}
Possible Responses:
- 200 OK
  {
    "token": "jwt_token_string",
    "name": "User Name",
    "isFirstTimeLogin": false,
    "message": "OTP verified, login successful",
    "role": "User",
    "otpRequired": false
  }
- 400 Bad Request
  { "Message": "Email and OTP are required." }
- 401 Unauthorized
  { "Message": "Invalid or expired OTP" }

3. POST /api/auth/forgot-password
Request Body:
{
  "email": "user@example.com"
}
Possible Responses:
- 200 OK
  "OTP sent to your email address"
- 400 Bad Request
  "Email is required"
- 404 Not Found
  "User not found"

4. POST /api/auth/reset-password
Request Body:
{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "otpCode": "123456",
  "newPassword": "newPassword123"
}
Possible Responses:
- 200 OK
  "Password reset successfully"
- 400 Bad Request
  "Email, OTP, and new password are required"
  or
  "Invalid or expired OTP, or user not found"

5. POST /api/auth/logout (Requires Authorization)
Headers:
Authorization: Bearer <jwt_token>
Possible Responses:
- 200 OK
  "Logged out successfully"

Example Data and Scenarios

Login
- Valid: Existing user, correct password.
- Invalid: Wrong password, inactive account, missing fields.

Verify OTP
- Valid: Correct OTP sent to email.
- Invalid: Wrong OTP, expired OTP, missing fields.

Forgot Password
- Valid: Registered email.
- Invalid: Unregistered email, missing email.

Reset Password
- Valid: Correct OTP, new password.
- Invalid: Wrong/expired OTP, missing fields, unregistered email.

Logout
- Valid: Valid JWT token in header.
